From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: stop audio before the main link goes idle

On unplug, msm_dp_bridge_atomic_disable() pushes the main link to idle
and only msm_dp_display_disable(), in post_disable, waits for the audio
stream to close. Userspace closes it about 450 ms later, so the ADSP's
DisplayPort sink keeps running into an idle link. On the TB321FU (SM8650,
AudioReach) the next DisplayPort start then fails: GRAPH_START on port
104 answers after ~500 ms with status 1 and the APM stops answering for
~15 s. Plugs alternated with and without audio.

Lenovo's kernel for this board turns audio off and waits before the
stream pre-disable (dp_display_pre_disable(), dp_display_process_hpd_low()).
Do the same: signal the unplug to audio and wait for audio_comp in
atomic_disable, before PUSH_IDLE. post_disable's wait then returns at
once. Tested: 10 plugs, all with audio (before: about one in two muted).

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -1422,6 +1422,19 @@
 
 	msm_dp_display = container_of(dp, struct msm_dp_display_private, msm_dp_display);
 
+	/*
+	 * Let the audio stream stop while the main link still carries it. If
+	 * the link goes idle first, the ADSP's DisplayPort sink keeps running
+	 * into it and its next start times out. Lenovo's driver also turns
+	 * audio off before the stream's pre-disable.
+	 */
+	if (dp->power_on && dp->audio_enabled) {
+		msm_dp_display_handle_plugged_change(dp, false);
+		if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&msm_dp_display->audio_comp,
+						 HZ * 5))
+			DRM_ERROR("audio comp timeout\n");
+	}
+
 	msm_dp_ctrl_push_idle(msm_dp_display->ctrl);
 }
 
